---
import Icon from "./Icon.astro";
import {defaults,series} from '../lib/model.ts';
interface Props {standalone?:boolean}
const {standalone=false}=Astro.props;
const Title=standalone?"h2":"h3";
const curve=series(defaults).map((p,i)=>`${i?'L':'M'}${28+p.time/60*560},${181-p.product*160}`).join(' ');
const grid=Array.from({length:5},(_,i)=>`<line x1="28" x2="588" y1="${181-i*40}" y2="${181-i*40}"/><text x="0" y="${184-i*40}">${(i/4).toFixed(2)}</text>`).join('');
---
<section data-lab data-standalone={standalone?"true":undefined} id="lab" class="lab dark section-pad" aria-labelledby={standalone?"page-title":"lab-title"}>
      {!standalone&&<>
      <div class="section-kicker mono"><span>02 / THE LAB</span><span><i class="status-dot"></i> INTERACTIVE DEMO</span></div>
      <div class="section-heading"><h2 id="lab-title">Less memorising.<br>More <span class="serif">“what if?”</span></h2><p>Change a variable. Follow the evidence.<br>Understanding begins when you get involved.</p></div>
      </>}
      <div class="lab-shell">
        <div class="lab-toolbar"><div><span class="mono tag">CHEMISTRY</span><Title>Reaction rates</Title></div><span class="mono experiment-id">EXPERIMENT / 001<br>A → B · FIRST-ORDER PROXY</span></div>
        <div class="lab-workspace">
          <div class="lab-visuals">
            <div class="particle-panel"><canvas id="particle-canvas" role="img" aria-label="Illustrative reactant and product particles. Lavender rings represent reactant A; green dots represent product B. Position and motion are not molecular dynamics."></canvas><div class="particle-legend mono"><span><i class="reactant-dot"></i> REACTANT A</span><span><i class="product-dot"></i> PRODUCT B</span></div><button disabled type="button" data-lab-motion class="particle-motion" aria-label="Pause particle animation" aria-pressed="false"><Icon name="pause"/></button><span class="particle-note mono">ILLUSTRATIVE PARTICLE VIEW</span></div>
            <div class="graph-panel"><div class="graph-heading mono"><span>PRODUCT CONCENTRATION / mol dm⁻³</span><span class="graph-key"><i></i> SELECTED <i></i> REFERENCE</span></div><svg id="rate-graph" viewBox="0 0 600 200" role="img" aria-labelledby="graph-title graph-description"><title id="graph-title">Product concentration over model time</title><desc id="graph-description">The green curve shows the selected conditions. A dashed curve shows the reference: 25 degrees Celsius, one mole per cubic decimetre, relative area one, no catalyst.</desc><g id="graph-grid" set:html={grid}/><path id="graph-fill" d={`${curve} L588,181 L28,181 Z`}/><path id="graph-baseline" d={curve}/><path id="graph-curve" d={curve}/><line id="graph-cursor"/><circle id="graph-point" cx="28" cy="181" r="4"/></svg><div class="graph-bottom mono"><span>0</span><span>MODEL TIME / s</span><span>60</span></div></div>
            <div class="lab-readouts"><div><span class="mono">MODEL TIME</span><output aria-live="off" id="time-output">0.0 <small>s</small></output></div><div><span class="mono">PRODUCT [B]</span><output aria-live="off" id="product-output">0.000 <small>mol dm⁻³</small></output></div><div><span class="mono">INITIAL RATE / REF.</span><output aria-live="off" id="relative-output">1.00<small>×</small></output></div></div>
          </div>
          <form id="lab-controls" class="lab-controls"><noscript><p class="no-js-note">The graph shows the reference model. Enable JavaScript to change conditions and run the experiment.</p></noscript>
            <div class="control-intro mono"><span>THE VARIABLES</span><span aria-hidden="true"><svg class="ui-icon" data-icon="arrow-down-right" viewBox="0 0 24 24" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><use href="#icon-arrow-down-right"></use></svg></span></div>
            <div class="variable"><div><label for="temperature">Temperature</label><output aria-live="off" for="temperature" id="temperature-output">25 °C</output></div><input disabled type="range" id="temperature" min="10" max="60" step="1" value="25"><div class="range-extents mono"><span>10 °C</span><span>60 °C</span></div></div>
            <div class="variable"><div><label for="concentration">Initial concentration</label><output aria-live="off" for="concentration" id="concentration-output">1.00 mol dm⁻³</output></div><input disabled type="range" id="concentration" min="0.25" max="2" step="0.05" value="1"><div class="range-extents mono"><span>0.25 mol dm⁻³</span><span>2.00 mol dm⁻³</span></div></div>
            <div class="variable"><div><label for="area">Relative surface area</label><output aria-live="off" for="area" id="area-output">1.0×</output></div><input disabled type="range" id="area" min="1" max="4" step="0.1" value="1"><div class="range-extents mono"><span>1×</span><span>4×</span></div></div>
            <label class="catalyst-control" for="catalyst"><span>Catalyst<small>Explore a lower activation barrier</small></span><input disabled id="catalyst" type="checkbox"><span class="switch" aria-hidden="true"></span></label>
            <div class="lab-buttons"><button disabled id="run-lab" type="button" class="button primary">Run experiment <span aria-hidden="true"><svg class="ui-icon" data-icon="arrow-up-right" viewBox="0 0 24 24" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><use href="#icon-arrow-up-right"></use></svg></span></button><button disabled id="reset-lab" type="reset" class="reset-button" aria-label="Reset all experiment controls and time"><svg class="ui-icon" data-icon="reset" viewBox="0 0 24 24" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><use href="#icon-reset"></use></svg> Reset</button></div>
            <p id="lab-status" role="status" class="mono">READY. MAKE A PREDICTION, THEN RUN.</p>
          </form>
        </div>
        <div class="lab-foot"><span class="mono">CHANGE CONDITIONS TO START A FRESH RUN.</span><button disabled id="export-csv" class="text-link">Download model data <span aria-hidden="true"><svg class="ui-icon" data-icon="arrow-down" viewBox="0 0 24 24" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><use href="#icon-arrow-down"></use></svg></span></button></div>
      </div>
      <details class="model-details"><summary><span class="mono">READ THE MODEL, ASSUMPTIONS & SOURCES</span><span class="cross" aria-hidden="true">+</span></summary><div class="model-detail-grid"><div><h4>A transparent simplification.</h4><p>This is an illustrative heterogeneous, first-order A → B proxy, not a model fitted to a specific reaction. It assumes constant temperature, constant effective surface area, and no reverse reaction.</p><p>Changing initial concentration scales initial rate and final product, but does not change the first-order rate constant. Surface area is an explicit linear multiplier for this proxy; it is not a universal rate law.</p></div><div><p class="formula">[B](t) = [A]₀(1 − e<sup>−kt</sup>)</p><p>k = S · A · exp(−Eₐ/RT), with R = 8.314 J mol⁻¹ K⁻¹. A is calibrated so k = 0.035 s⁻¹ at 25 °C, S = 1, Eₐ = 40 kJ mol⁻¹. The catalyst option uses Eₐ = 35 kJ mol⁻¹ with the same A. These values are illustrative.</p><p>Particle motion is a visual aid, not a collision calculation. Animation speed is not a measured reaction rate. The dashed reference always uses the default conditions.</p><a href="https://goldbook.iupac.org/terms/view/A00446" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class="text-link">Source: IUPAC · Arrhenius equation <svg class="ui-icon" data-icon="arrow-up-right" viewBox="0 0 24 24" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><use href="#icon-arrow-up-right"></use></svg></a><br><a href="https://edu.rsc.org/cpd/teaching-rates-of-reaction-post-16-part-2/4014195.article" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class="text-link">Source: Royal Society of Chemistry · Catalysis <svg class="ui-icon" data-icon="arrow-up-right" viewBox="0 0 24 24" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><use href="#icon-arrow-up-right"></use></svg></a></div></div></details>
    </section>
<script>import "../scripts/lab-loader.ts";</script>
